WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:21.275
The Prince's words cut deeply into the Little Mermaid's heart.

2
00:00:21.276 --> 00:00:24.573
All her hopes and dreams were shattered.

3
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:31.452
Unable to speak, she could not tell the Prince she had saved him from the storm.

4
00:00:31.453 --> 00:00:36.027
There was no way to tell him that she would die if he married the Maiden.

5
00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:40.429
Without a voice she couldn't utter a single word.

6
00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.916
"What have I done?" she thought.

7
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:48.411
"I should never have given my voice to the witch."

8
00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:54.087
The Little Mermaid could not even weep with sorrow, since mermaids cannot cry.

9
00:00:54.088 --> 00:00:58.086
She could only look at the Prince with her sad eyes.

10
00:00:58.087 --> 00:01:04.357
Blinded by his own happiness, the Prince could not see that he had broken her heart.

11
00:01:04.358 --> 00:01:09.143
"I never thought that I would find my Maiden," he said happily.

12
00:01:09.144 --> 00:01:13.554
"My dear little companion, you will share in my great joy."

13
00:01:13.555 --> 00:01:20.644
The following day royal guards rode through the streets announcing the marriage.

14
00:01:20.645 --> 00:01:28.003
Then the members of the royal families marched through town until they reached the center square.

15
00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:33.347
There the Prince and Princess Maiden joined hands and were wed.

16
00:01:33.348 --> 00:01:39.171
The young couple beamed with happiness, and the crowd cheered when they kissed.

17
00:01:39.172 --> 00:01:45.771
Only the Little Mermaid was heartsick as she held the bride's flowers during the ceremony.

18
00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:51.597
She thought about her old life in the Sea Kingdom and her grandmother's loving touch.

19
00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:56.740
"I have given up my home and family forever," she thought.

20
00:01:56.741 --> 00:02:00.108
"I have lost my lovely voice.

21
00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:04.078
And now I have lost my Prince.

22
00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:10.002
I will die the moment the sun rises over the sea."

23
00:02:10.003 --> 00:02:14.835
That evening the celebration continued on the grand ship.

24
00:02:14.836 --> 00:02:21.262
The Prince, his new bride, and all their guests went aboard for a huge party.

25
00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:27.668
It was a calm, clear night—just like the night the Little Mermaid had first seen the Prince.

26
00:02:27.669 --> 00:02:31.506
Brightly colored lanterns lit up the deck.

27
00:02:31.507 --> 00:02:35.506
Fireworks and cannon booms filled the air.

28
00:02:35.507 --> 00:02:40.472
Sailors and guests danced together to the lively music.

29
00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:45.886
The Prince walked over to the Little Mermaid, bowed, and asked,

30
00:02:45.887 --> 00:02:51.516
"My little companion, will you do me the honor of dancing for my guests?"

31
00:02:51.517 --> 00:02:56.815
"I wish I could dance with you, my Prince," she wanted to say.

32
00:02:56.816 --> 00:03:01.918
Instead the Little Mermaid spun onto the floor alone.

33
00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:07.228
As always her tender feet hurt terribly.

34
00:03:07.229 --> 00:03:12.760
But this time she did not notice the pain because her heart was broken.

35
00:03:12.761 --> 00:03:18.668
She knew this would be her last night on earth, and she would never see her Prince again.

36
00:03:18.669 --> 00:03:25.847
The Little Mermaid would not get a soul but instead become foam upon the waves.

37
00:03:25.848 --> 00:03:33.454
She danced as if she were under a spell—without thought, without dreams, without hope.

38
00:03:33.455 --> 00:03:36.815
The guests cheered at her every step and turn.

39
00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:39.396
Her feet seemed enchanted.

40
00:03:39.397 --> 00:03:44.444
Finally the music stopped, and so did the Little Mermaid.

41
00:03:44.445 --> 00:03:48.596
She looked for the Prince, but he had left.

42
00:03:48.597 --> 00:03:51.206
"The happy couple has gone to bed,"

43
00:03:51.207 --> 00:03:56.055
said one of the guests, as if in answer to her thoughts.

44
00:03:56.056 --> 00:03:58.538
"Let us wish them well!"

45
00:03:58.539 --> 00:04:03.212
On the deck a tent of golden silk had been set up.

46
00:04:03.213 --> 00:04:07.593
Inside the tent the royal pair sat on a bed.

47
00:04:07.594 --> 00:04:20.507
As the guests cheered, the Prince kissed his bride and ran his fingers through her hair.
